<title>EGYPT: Egyptian money supply grows 10.7 pct to Dec 1996.</title>
<headline>Egyptian money supply grows 10.7 pct to Dec 1996.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian broad money supply grew 10.7 percent in the year to the end of December 1996, from 10.5 in the year to November and 10.5 to the end of December 1995, according to International Monetary Fund statistics.</p>
<p>Total money supply, including quasi-money and foreign currency deposits, was 180.133 billion pounds at the end of December, against 178.642 billion pounds at the end of November.</p>
<p>				 Dec 96	Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p> Money			 44.251	44.595	41.540</p>
<p> Quasi-money		135.882     134.047     121.227</p>
<p> Total money supply     180.133     178.642     162.767</p>
<p>     Month-on-month	+0.83	 +0.65	 +0.72</p>
<p>     Year-on-year	 +10.67	+10.54	+10.49</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
